# SECTION 13 — PERFORMANCE, CACHING AND RATE LIMITS

The existing application experienced repeated library reads, excessive signed-URL requests and rate-limit errors.

Preserve and improve the performance fixes already implemented.

## 13.1 Cached library reads

- Reuse cached library reads across pages.
- Avoid repeatedly fetching the same library on every mount.
- Load Photos once per appropriate session or cache lifecycle.
- Apply filters locally when the cached data is sufficient.
- Refresh or invalidate cached data after uploads.
- Refresh after deletions.
- Refresh after moves.
- Refresh after sharing.
- Refresh after revocations.
- Clear account-specific cached data when signing out or switching accounts.

## 13.2 Signed URL management

- Limit concurrent signing requests.
- Avoid unnecessary signed URL creation.
- Reuse valid signed URLs only within their permitted lifetime.
- Handle expired signed URLs.
- Retry temporary failures safely.
- Avoid infinite retry loops.

## 13.3 Rate-limit handling

When a rate-limit response occurs:

- Do not crash the application.
- Display a friendly Try Again card.
- Preserve the user's current page.
- Avoid aggressive repeated retries.
- Provide meaningful error messages.
- Allow a safe retry when appropriate.

## 13.4 Performance optimization

- Use pagination for large libraries.
- Use lazy loading.
- Load thumbnails before full-resolution images.
- Avoid duplicate API requests.
- Optimize gallery rendering.
- Avoid unnecessary component updates.
- Keep the application responsive.

